# What the Vercel CLI uploads.
#
# Vercel runs the application itself: FastAPI, the templates, the articles,
# the static assets, and the build step that bakes the embedding model into
# the bundle. Nothing else in this repository belongs there.
#
# Default-deny, matching .gcloudignore and .dockerignore: nothing is
# uploaded unless it is named here. That way a new private file alongside
# this repository is never sent by accident, and no private path has to be
# named in this public file.
#
# Git-triggered deployments do not use this file -- they build from the
# repository, which contains none of those private directories in the first
# place. This is the guard for `vercel deploy` from a working tree.
/*

# The application
!/server.py
!/config.py
!/security.py
!/content.py
!/blog.py
!/search.py

# Dependencies, the build step, and the platform configuration
!/requirements.txt
!/vercel_build.py
!/vercel.json
!/.python-version

# Templates, static assets, and the articles
!/templates
!/assets
!/content
